---
// Credits and disclaimer (roadmap Phase 1). Every claim here names a source
// the site really uses; keep it in step with docs/api.md and ADR-0004/0007.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_DESCRIPTION, ARCHIVE_FIRST_SEASON } from '../config/site.js'
---
<Base title="About and credits" description={`Where the data on ${SITE_NAME} comes from, and who owns it.`}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About and credits</h1>
    <p>{SITE_DESCRIPTION}</p>

    <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not run, approved or endorsed by Major League Baseball, Minor League Baseball, the
      Milwaukee Brewers or any affiliate club. Team names, logos and player photos belong to their owners.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Rosters, player bios and stats:</strong> the MLB Stats API (statsapi.mlb.com), © MLB Advanced
        Media, L.P. The site copies it once a night. A prospect card in a post reads it again in your browser.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Team logos and player photos:</strong> loaded from MLB's own servers (mlbstatic.com). The site
        does not copy or change them.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Current Brewers prospect ranks:</strong> MLB Pipeline, on MLB.com.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Top 100 history:</strong> Baseball America's lists for {ARCHIVE_FIRST_SEASON} to 2008, and MLB
        Pipeline's from 2009.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Minor-league data is often thin. Where a value is missing, the site shows a dash or "not on record" rather
      than a guess.
    </p>

    <h2>Errors and requests</h2>
    <p>
      If something is wrong, or you own something here and want it removed, open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/gzilavyss2025/brewprospects/issues">the site's GitHub repository</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      The site's code is open source under the
      <a href="https://github.com/gzilavyss2025/brewprospects/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a>. That license
      covers the code only: not the posts, and not the data, logos or photos from the sources above.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
